<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African govt financing 3.34 bln rand in January.</title>
<headline>S.African govt financing 3.34 bln rand in January.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Government financing amounted to 3.34 billion rand in January after it raised 2.61 billion rand in the bond markets while net short-term loans increased by 727 million rand, the Department of Finance said.</p>
<p>Government bonds and debentures totalling 15,913 million rand and foreign loans of 750 million rand were redeemed during the financial year April 1996 to January 1997. Total</p>
<p>budgeted financing is 45.1 billion rand for the year.</p>
<p>(rand million)		Jan '97   April-Jan	Budgeted 96/97</p>
<p>Government bonds</p>
<p>and debentures	  2,616.5   32,643.4	 39,604.7</p>
<p>Short-term (net):</p>
<p>  Bridging bonds	    0.0   -3,676.5	 -3,616.5</p>
<p>  Tender bills	    827.6    3,200.4	  3,616.5</p>
<p>  CPD			 -99.9    1,595.0	  3,000.0</p>
<p>Foreign loans		 0.0    2,831.0	  2,500.0</p>
<p>Total financing	 3,344.2   36,592.9	 45,104.7</p>
<p>((  -- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003 ))</p>
